# Hemp planks door -- the two block halves plus the item icon.
#
# Drawn as one 16x32 sheet so the stiles, the rails and the plank grain line up
# across the block seam by construction; the base grain is hemp_planks.png tiled
# twice, so a door reads as the same wood as the block it is crafted from.
#
# The depth comes from one rule, applied to every opening and to the lower
# panel: the lip ABOVE a hole is the darkest tone and the lip BELOW it is the
# lightest, with the left lip dark and the right lip light. That is what vanilla
# does around a door's window panes, and it is the whole difference between a
# window and a hole punched in a board.
#
# The window is a cutout cannabis leaf: five leaflets, the outer pair short, the
# sinuses between them cut as diagonal teeth that converge on the petiole. Keep
# the teeth attached to the frame -- a tooth that touches wood only diagonally
# is a loose pixel floating in mid-air once the block is see-through.
#
# The [note] about a dark border is accepted knowingly: a door IS a framed
# object, and the frame is the point.
#
#   python3 .claude/skills/minecraft-texture-painter/scripts/mctex.py render \
#     textures-src/hemp_planks_door.mctex \
#     -o src/main/resources/assets/hempdustry/textures --preview --preview-dir /tmp/tex

@palette hemp
. = none
k = 3E3A26      outer edge, darkest
o = 4E4830      groove, and the shadowed lip of every recess
d = 5A5236      plank shadow
e = 67603E      plank dark
m = 82794E      plank mid
b = 8A8155
g = 948A5E
h = A1976C
w = A89D73      lit lip of every recess
n = 4E525A      iron, shadow
i = 6B6F7A      iron
I = 8C939C      iron, lit

@sheet door_sheet 16x32 palette=hemp
oghwwwwwhwwwwwho
ohggmbghhhgghhbo
ohhhghgoobbgghho
